      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "hello im here today to say the issue was fixed. thank god. first of all this website and everything about it from support to what even else is extremely poor. from mods 'snip' my post to just being plain usless in helping me solve this issue. i dont care i posted this on the 30th of july and its now the 11th of September with 0 reply so anywheres maybe its was not a normal thing. i truly dont know what i fixed the issue for me but here are the things that was done was check for corrupted system files. both DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth and sfc /scannow was done. i them made sure that my firewall wasnt blocking the youtube-dl.exe. when i check the event viewer i saw a something for vrchat and UnityPlayer.dll but no fixes i found online helped. i keep getting drivers and windows updates as time went by so idk if this fixed the issue but about 3 days ago i was installing samsung smart switch and it requested me to install something called windows media feture pack. it could be the latest nvidia driver from a few days ago or the windows update or the windows media feature pack i downloaded that seem to fixed the issue. up till now im not sure what fixed it. its has to be one of these cause everything was up to date, latest youtube-dl and all also clean install. last time it worked was before i reinstalled windows until now.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
